<div class="min-h-screen bg-paper text-ink font-plex antialiased">
  <.patient_header back={~p"/"} back_label="Back to home">
    <div class="text-center text-[13.5px] font-semibold text-ink-muted">Privacy and terms</div>
  </.patient_header>

  <main class="max-w-[720px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 pb-16">
    <article class="bg-white border border-line rounded-[20px] px-6 py-7 sm:px-10 sm:py-9 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-muted [&_h2]:font-display [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-8 [&_h2]:mb-2 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ul]:space-y-1">
      <h1 class="font-display font-semibold text-[30px] leading-tight text-ink mb-3">
        How CareRoute uses your information
      </h1>
      <p>
        CareRoute AI is a hackathon prototype that helps you choose the right level of care. It
        is a navigator, not a diagnostic tool, and it does not replace a clinician. If this may
        be an emergency, call 999 or 112 (Kenya) now.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          What you type or say in the chat, and the optional name, age and phone number you
          give. Your phone number is only for the facility you choose to contact you.
        </li>
        <li>The recommendation CareRoute makes and the facility you choose.</li>
        <li>The time you agreed to this notice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who sees it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Clinicians at the facility you choose see your answers, an AI summary, and the
          recommendation, so they can prepare for your visit.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your answers are sent to an AI service (Google Gemini, or Anthropic Claude as a
          backup) to decide the next question and write the clinician summary.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you answer by voice, your browser's speech service turns speech into text. In
          Chrome this sends the audio to Google.
        </li>
        <li>
          The map loads tiles from OpenStreetMap. If you share your location, it's used only
          during your visit to find the nearest facilities and isn't stored.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you search for a town instead, only the place name you type is sent to
          OpenStreetMap's Nominatim service to find it on the map.
        </li>
        <li>
          The facility directory comes from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors).
          Only facilities marked "CareRoute partner" receive referrals; for others, call ahead
          or go directly.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Conversations, recommendations and referrals are deleted automatically 30 days after
        you start. This is a demo system, so data may also be deleted sooner, for example
        before each rehearsal. Please don't use it for a real medical situation.
      </p>

      <h2 id="terms" class="scroll-mt-6">Terms of use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>CareRoute gives navigation suggestions only; it does not diagnose or treat.</li>
        <li>Always follow the advice of a clinician over CareRoute's suggestion.</li>
        <li>In an emergency, call 999 or 112 instead of using CareRoute.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or problems: open an issue at <a
          href="https://github.com/martin34524/care-route"
          class="text-route font-semibold underline underline-offset-2"
        >
          github.com/martin34524/care-route
        </a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</div>
